---
description: Vector architecture boundaries
alwaysApply: true
---
Vector is a modular monolith with explicit Control Plane and Delivery Plane boundaries.
Use TypeScript, Bun, Svelte 5/SvelteKit, Hono, PostgreSQL, Drizzle.
Package manager is Bun, never npm.
PostgreSQL is durable business state. Redis is transient. Trigger.dev owns production jobs.
Cursor Automations are not the marketing runtime.
Keep external vendors behind adapters.
One Delivery Plane serves many client custom domains. Do not deploy an app per client.
MGE website and Vector application are separate products.
Control Plane is authenticated. Delivery Plane is public. Do not mix those security postures.
Public Delivery experiences follow `docs/27`. Do not clone reference sites or generate generic AI marketing pages.
Vector 24 measures Vector Ready to live, not contract signing to live.
Do not implement the entire roadmap. Phase 0 first, then vertical slices.
Do not add infrastructure because it is fashionable. Require an ADR for new major infrastructure.
